  "notes": "{後悔|こうかい} means regret or remorse about past actions or decisions.\n\nKANJI BREAKDOWN:\n{後|こう} (after) + {悔|かい} (regret) = 'after-regret'\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {後悔|こうかい}する: to regret\n- {後悔|こうかい}の{念|ねん}: feeling of regret\n- {後悔|こうかい}のない{人生|じんせい}: life without regrets\n- {深|ふか}く{後悔|こうかい}する: to deeply regret\n\nFAMOUS PROVERB:\n{後悔|こうかい}{先|さき}に{立|た}たず\n'Regret doesn't stand before' → No use crying over spilt milk\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {反省|はんせい}: self-reflection, introspection\n- {悔|く}やむ: to regret (verb)\n- {残念|ざんねん}: disappointment, regrettable",
